// Mount Oros: Aigina's peak (Act II).
// design/phase2/SCRIPT.md, "Aegina's interior: an optional detour". The map and
// every event's place come from tools/ichor/maps/aegina_detour.py.
//
// The path climbs from the road through the pines and a band of golden grass to
// the summit, where King Aiakos prayed for rain at Zeus's altar and ended a
// drought for all of Greece. A jar of Wine waits beside it (Zeus's offering;
// ICHOR_STUB_OFFERINGS: the ball holds Berry Juice until the engine adds Wine).
// The sea is on every side but the road's.

mapscripts AeginaMountOros_MapScripts {}

// ICHOR_STUB_RITES: ENGINE_API section 3's EventScript_IchorAltar_Zeus isn't on
// this branch. When it lands, point the altar's bg event straight at it.
script AeginaMountOros_EventScript_AltarOfZeus {
    msgbox(format("An altar of Zeus on the island's peak. A cloud is sitting on the summit.\p"
                  "From here you can see Emporion's masts, and the mountains behind them.\p"
                  "And far out to sea, if you squint and lie a little, Kalliste."), MSGBOX_SIGN)
}
